[/table]

[h2]🔗 Load order with other mods[/h2]
In the Paradox Launcher the mod [b]lower[/b] in the playset loads later and wins any file both mods change.
[table]
[tr][th]Mod[/th][th]Order[/th][th]Notes[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]Millennium Dawn[/td][td]MD above, FPS Map below[/td][td]Tested with 2.0.3. Don't use the Calm Water Add-on with MD.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3816496697]Globe Mod[/url][/td][td]FPS Map above, Globe below[/td][td]The globe works fully. FPS Map keeps everything except its flat arrow shading, far-zoom river snow and shallow-sea tint (Globe needs those shaders). Don't use the Calm Water Add-on with Globe.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Original FPS Map (Mlecz)[/td][td]✖ Disable it[/td][td]Same files; this mod replaces it.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]UI, unit, flag, focus and overhaul mods[/td][td]Any order[/td][td]Checked: Historical Army Insignia and Focus Tree Swapper share no files; Hearts of Iron: 1984 Revived shares 3 icons (the lower mod's icon art shows).[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Other shader / map-graphics mods[/td][td]Your choice[/td][td]If both change the same file, the lower mod wins that file; the rest of FPS Map still applies.[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[b]Why is it Ironman & MP safe?[/b] The game checksum only covers [i]common/, events/, history/[/i] and map data files. This mod touches none of them — only shaders, textures and arrow visuals — so your checksum stays identical to vanilla (verified in game).

[hr][/hr]

[h2]🛠 What was fixed compared to the original[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Crash / broken arrows fixed:[/b] the map-arrow shader was an outdated copy missing three effects the engine now requires (raid arrows, see-through plan arrows). Rebuilt from the 1.19 shader with the mod's style re-applied.
[*][b]HQ / general connection lines restored:[/b] 12 arrow and symbol types added in recent patches (deployed-general front lines, commander ability range, raid arrows) were missing and simply did not draw.
[*][b]Invalid reflection texture replaced:[/b] the water/sky reflection was a flat image where the game expects a cube map. Now a proper (black) cube map — same look, no rendering errors.
[*][b]Stretched UI bars fixed:[/b] deployment and fuel bars resized to the current UI slots.
[*][b]Smoother scaled icons:[/b] 10 map/UI icons now carry full mip chains like vanilla.
[*][b]Cleanup:[/b] 15 obsolete or unused files removed.
[/list]
Every changed file is rebuilt from the [i]current[/i] vanilla file with only the mod's own edits applied, so nothing new from Paradox is lost.

[hr][/hr]

