[h2]📦 Installation[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe.
[*]In the Paradox Launcher, add [b]FPS Map - Updated for 1.19 (Ironman & MP Safe)[/b] to your playset.
[*][b]Disable the original FPS Map[/b] if you have it — both replace the same files.
[/olist]

[h2]❓ FAQ[/h2]
[b]Will it really raise my FPS?[/b]
It removes per-pixel work from water, rivers and arrows; the gain is largest on mid-range and laptop GPUs in big wars. It won't fix CPU-bound late-game slowdowns — that is the simulation, not the map.

[b]Does it change gameplay?[/b]
No. Purely visual.

[b]Can I use it with other UI / map mods?[/b]
Yes — see the load order guide above. Put the mod you want to win lower in the playset.

[b]Sea and land regions show names like "STRATEGICREGION_49" — is this mod broken?[/b]
No — FPS Map ships no text. The debug map editor (Nudger) left files in your user folder that override every mod. Move the contents of the [i]localisation[/i] and [i]map[/i] folders in [i]Documents/Paradox Interactive/Hearts of Iron IV/[/i] somewhere else (keep a copy). A leftover [i]map/unitstacks.txt[/i] there also changes your checksum and blocks Ironman achievements.

